1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:01,895
Good morning.

2
00:00:01,895 --> 00:00:03,985
Welcome to the Early Learning Childcare Centre.

3
00:00:03,985 --> 00:00:05,560
How may I help you?

4
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:05,837
Hi.

5
00:00:05,837 --> 00:00:09,440
I spoke to you last week about enrolling my daughter for next year.

6
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,273
Oh, yes.

7
00:00:10,273 --> 00:00:13,190
I'll just get some details from you.

8
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:14,857
So, you're her mother?

9
00:00:14,857 --> 00:00:15,690
That's right.

10
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:17,790
And, can I have your name?

11
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:19,190
It's Carol, Carol Smith.

12
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:21,237
And your daughter's name?

13
00:00:21,237 --> 00:00:22,260
It's Kate.

14
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:26,932
Now, we have several groups at the centre and we cater for children from

15
00:00:26,932 --> 00:00:28,601
three to five years old.

16
00:00:28,601 --> 00:00:30,270
How old is your daughter?

17
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:33,800
She's three now but she turns four next month.

18
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,770
I'll put four down because that's how old she'll be when she starts.

19
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:41,240
Fine, she's so excited about her birthday and coming to the centre.

20
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:43,310
That's good to hear.

21
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:45,380
And what's your address?

22
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:50,350
It's 46 Wombat Road,

23
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:52,835
that's W-O-M-B-A-T.

24
00:00:52,835 --> 00:00:55,320
Woodside 4032.

25
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:59,770
And what's the phone number?

26
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:00,660
Oh ...

27
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,550
it's ...

28
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:03,330
3345 9865.

29
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:07,700
So, have you decided on the days you'd like to bring your daughter here?

30
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,960
I'd prefer Monday and Wednesday if possible.

31
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:11,523
Mmm.

32
00:01:11,523 --> 00:01:13,775
I'll check, Monday's fine,

33
00:01:13,775 --> 00:01:19,404
but I think the centre is already full for Wednesday.

34
00:01:19,404 --> 00:01:19,967
Erm.

35
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:20,530
Yes.

36
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:20,842
Sorry.

37
00:01:20,842 --> 00:01:23,338
It seems to be a very popular day.

38
00:01:23,338 --> 00:01:26,770
We can offer you a Thursday or a Friday as well.

39
00:01:26,770 --> 00:01:27,553
Oh dear.

40
00:01:27,553 --> 00:01:32,640
I suppose Thursday would be all right because she has swimming on Friday.

41
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:33,769
OK, got that.

42
00:01:33,769 --> 00:01:39,040
Because a lot of parents work, we do offer flexible start and finish times.

43
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:43,569
We are open from 7:30 in the morning until 6 o'clock at night.

44
00:01:43,569 --> 00:01:46,480
What time would you like your daughter to start?

45
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:49,132
I need to get to work in the city by 9:00

46
00:01:49,132 --> 00:01:50,900
so I'll drop her off at 8:30.

47
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:54,501
You're pretty close to the city here so that should give me plenty of

48
00:01:54,501 --> 00:01:55,530
time to get there.

49
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:56,261
That's fine.

50
00:01:56,261 --> 00:02:00,280
Now, we also need to decide which group she'll be in.

51
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:04,400
We have two different groups and they're divided up according to age.

52
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,720
There's the green group,

53
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:08,360
which is for three to four year olds.

54
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:12,970
And then there's the red group which is for four- to five-year-olds.

55
00:02:12,970 --> 00:02:16,419
She's quite mature for her age and she can already write her name

56
00:02:16,419 --> 00:02:17,480
and read a little.

57
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:20,913
Well, I'll put her in the red group and we can always change her

58
00:02:20,913 --> 00:02:23,120
to the green one if there are any problems.

59
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,423
That sounds fine.

60
00:02:24,423 --> 00:02:24,858
OK.

61
00:02:24,858 --> 00:02:27,029
Let's move on to meals.

62
00:02:27,029 --> 00:02:30,070
We can provide breakfast, lunch and dinner.

63
00:02:30,070 --> 00:02:34,797
As she's finishing pretty early, she won't need dinner, will you give her breakfast

64
00:02:34,797 --> 00:02:35,810
before she comes?

65
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:39,940
Yes, she'll only need lunch.

66
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:44,110
Now, does she have any medical conditions we need to know about?

67
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:47,760
Does she have asthma or any hearing problems for example?

68
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:48,079
No.

69
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:50,315
But she does need to wear glasses.

70
00:02:50,315 --> 00:02:52,550
Oh, I'll make a note of that.

71
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:56,480
Yes, she's pretty good about wearing them, she can't see much without them.

72
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:57,029
Right.

73
00:02:57,029 --> 00:02:57,578
OK.

74
00:02:57,578 --> 00:03:01,420
Now, I also need emergency contact details.

75
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:04,130
So what sort of information do you need?

76
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:07,658
Just the name and number of a friend or family member we can contact

77
00:03:07,658 --> 00:03:10,430
in case we can't get hold of you at any time.

78
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:11,224
OK.

79
00:03:11,224 --> 00:03:15,191
That'd better be my sister...

80
00:03:15,191 --> 00:03:16,778
Jenny Ball.

81
00:03:16,778 --> 00:03:19,159
That's B-A-double L.

82
00:03:19,159 --> 00:03:23,920
Her phone number is 3346 7523.

83
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:24,374
Great.

84
00:03:24,374 --> 00:03:27,098
So she is the child's aunt?

85
00:03:27,098 --> 00:03:27,552
Yes,

86
00:03:27,552 --> 00:03:28,460
that's right.

87
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:30,920
I'll make a note of that as well.

88
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:33,380
Now, is there anything you'd like to ask?

89
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,517
What about payment?

90
00:03:34,517 --> 00:03:37,170
How much are the fees each term?

91
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:41,818
Well, for two days and the hours you've chosen,

92
00:03:41,818 --> 00:03:44,400
that will be $450 altogether.

93
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:44,741
OK,

94
00:03:44,741 --> 00:03:47,470
and do I have to pay that now?

95
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:51,420
No, we send out invoices once the children start at the centre.

96
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:54,550
You can choose to pay at the end of each term

97
00:03:54,550 --> 00:03:58,250
or we do offer a slightly discounted rate if you pay every month.

98
00:03:58,250 --> 00:03:58,520
Oh.

99
00:03:58,520 --> 00:03:59,598
I'll do that then.

100
00:03:59,598 --> 00:04:03,372
I find it easier to budget that way and I'm not used to the

101
00:04:03,372 --> 00:04:04,450
term dates just yet.

102
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:07,725
Good, it makes it a lot simpler for us as well.

103
00:04:07,725 --> 00:04:08,023
Well,

104
00:04:08,023 --> 00:04:08,618
that's everything.

105
00:04:08,618 --> 00:04:11,000
Would you like me to show you around …？
